WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:02.669
Forests tend to be naturally spooky places.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:07.750
They are dense with trees letting in little
light, and offering plenty of spots for predatory

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:12.769
animals to hide while stalking their prey---prey
that sometimes include humans.

00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:14.759
But life also thrives there.

00:00:14.759 --> 00:00:19.449
For the Slavic people, there’s one spirit
that rules it all, a lord of the woods—the

00:00:19.449 --> 00:00:20.449
Leshy.

00:00:20.449 --> 00:00:21.449
The leshy.

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:25.810
The leshy is a shape-shifting creature that
may appear human but also takes on the form

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.030
of the animals and plants he protects.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:32.910
He was once believed to lead travelers to
their deaths but could also insure a successful

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:33.910
hunt.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:37.450
He kidnapped young women but kept cattle from
getting lost in the woods.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.610
He was feared, but also revered.

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:44.879
The leshy isn’t just some high level boss
in a video game but an important, mischievous,

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:50.820
powerful spirit that can trace its history
back to ancient religious and cultural beliefs.

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.019
[Monstrum intro.]

00:00:54.019 --> 00:01:04.010
If you’ve ever been in the woods, you know
how scary they can be and how easy it can

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:05.509
be to get lost.

00:01:05.509 --> 00:01:10.080
In one 19thcentury text the leshy is directly
connected to the dangers of the forest.

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:16.690
It reads, “In olden days, when forests were
larger and denser than they are now, the Leshy

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:21.920
used to be constantly deluding travelers,
and making them lose their way.”

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.869
And no forest was safe.

00:01:23.869 --> 00:01:28.180
While Slavic folklore claimed each forest
had its own leshy, there could be more than

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.440
one.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:33.470
Territorial disputes between leshy were said
to be the cause of harsh storms, boulders

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:38.659
falling, or crashing trees—supernatural
explanations for real events.

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:43.950
Most often a leshy appears in its imposingly
tall human guise with long claws and shaggy

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:47.170
hair, sometimes with horns and cloven feet.

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:52.520
He can grow higher than the tree-tops or small
enough to hide behind a blade of grass.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:56.990
The leshy’s appearance is often inspired
by the vegetation of the forest, with bark-like

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:59.399
skin and a green beard or hair.

00:01:59.399 --> 00:02:04.080
Which makes sense given that his name comes
from the Russian word meaning forest.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.000
Leshy translates to “wood spirit” or “wood
demon.”

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:11.730
I had the opportunity to talk to one of my
favorite authors, Katherine Arden, whose done

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.770
a ton of research about Slavic folklore for
her Winternight trilogy.

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:22.730
He most often appears as a Russian peasant,
but with some slight slight oddities.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.180
He doesn't wear a belt.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:29.520
The left in Russian is associated with the
demonic so he crosses his caftan left over

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.520
right.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:34.010
He also inverts his shoes so he wears his
shoes in the wrong feet.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:40.730
He doesn't cast a shadow and he carries a
cudgel or an ax like a weapon that sort of

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:43.750
symbolizes his authority over the forest.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:48.410
A Leshy may take on a human from, and even
disguise itself as someone its victim knows.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:52.900
But it can inadvertently reveal its true nature
through small mistakes in their transformation

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:58.340
And since he can take the shape of anything
in his domain, a leshy may appear as anything

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:06.000
from bears and wolves to domestic cattle,
birds, a tree, even a whirlwind of leaves.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.160
A leshy can also alter its voice.

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:13.410
He might call out to his victims in a voice
they recognize, or whistle like the wind blowing

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.480
through the trees.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:18.910
Animal sounds, the rustle of leaves, and laughter
are also part of his verbal repertoire, which

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:23.010
he would then use to confuse and tempt victims.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.810
He was feared because he possessed the ability
to lead people and animals astray, forcing

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:32.310
them to die from exhaustion trying to find
their way home or misleading them to fall

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.040
into a ravine or swamp.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:38.700
Leshii were said to be great gamblers, playing
cards against one another and other spirit

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.940
demons frequently, betting the resources of
their particular woods.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:47.680
When huge populations of squirrels suddenly
migrated across the Ural Mountains in the

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:53.180
19th century, some people attributed it to
a Siberian leshy driving its losses to their

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.840
“European kin.”

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:58.940
The leshy received sacrifices and offerings
from the people in order to secure his favor

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.200
and aid in their survival.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.750
As the master and guardian of the forest,
a huntsman’s success or a woodcutter’s

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:10.420
bounty was believed to be dependent on the
will of the leshy.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:12.830
Even herdsmen relied on this creature.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:17.100
Because of this relationship the herdsmen
were seen as intermediaries between the human

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:21.230
world and the world of the leshy—the spirit
world.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:26.650
You could avoid offending the leshy by respecting
the forest, not only in terms of taking resources,

00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:32.230
but in general modes of deference like not
whistling or swearing, and not intentionally

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:33.840
harming plants.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.210
Hunting on certain festival days was also
forbidden to avoid the leshy’s wrath.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:42.590
Laying out the traditional meal for greeting
important guests, bread with salt, on a tree

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.070
stump might keep you safe from the leshy.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:50.120
This seems pretty minor but it was, and in
some Slavic countries still is, a very important

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.330
gesture.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:52.480
Bread was synonymous with food.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.340
If a household didn’t have it, they didn’t
have the resources to eat.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:05:01.060
And salt was a rare commodity so sharing it
expressed hospitality.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:05.410
Other protections against leshy included making
the sign of the cross, saying a prayer or

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:10.020
spell, wearing clothes backwards or inside
out, &nbsp;retracing your steps out of the forest,

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:12.500
or making the leshy laugh,

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:16.790
So although Slavic folklore describes them
as antagonistic towards humans by nature,

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.620
you can win one over with a little respect.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:22.940
They can actually seem pretty reasonable in
a lot of ways.

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:27.630
Unfortunately, we can’t know the exact origins
of the legend since there is no record of

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:31.110
any Slavic mythology, which was honestly a
shock to me.

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:35.900
Many scholars agree that nothing about the
original Slavic gods, creation myths, or stories

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:38.360
of their afterlife has survived history.

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:42.630
The earliest records of the Slavs dates back
to only the 6th century.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:46.110
Around that time, the Slavs migrated into
other territories and developed into different

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.110
cultures.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:51.710
But one of the things they kept in common
is their folklore - including stories of the

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:52.710
leshy.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:57.170
It’s likely oral tradition played a huge
role in this story’s early creation.

00:05:57.170 --> 00:06:01.230
In fact, “Slavs” comes from the proto-Slavic
slovo [слово; English:“word”], meaning

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:04.840
that the people called themselves “those
who speak with words.”

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:09.620
However, it’s speculated that the Leshy
was later heavily influenced by Christianity.

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:14.550
As Christianity spread it sort of mingled
with paganism and local folklore.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:20.360
And there’s also sort of a Christian explanation
which says that the Leshy and other forest

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:26.320
household spirits were angels, that were thrown
from heaven after the war between angels.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:29.900
They fell to earth and became forest spirits.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:34.740
Or the other one is that spirits like the
Leshy are the children of Adam and Eve, born

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:40.740
after the fall of man but they went away - because
they were ashamed and were shamed, and they

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:42.389
became spirits of the forest.

00:06:42.389 --> 00:06:46.889
What was once simply a guardian of the forest
became a more devilish figure.

00:06:46.889 --> 00:06:51.370
This explains some leshy traits like the cloven
hooves, which are often associated with evil

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:53.250
deities in Christian stories.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:57.863
And even in some variations of the monster,
a leshy is created from the marriage of the

00:06:57.863 --> 00:07:01.650
Devil and a witch or they can be descendants
of Satan’s army.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:06.870
A hunter or herdsmen could secure safety and
success by creating a pact with the creature,

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:10.639
an act that required renouncing Christianity.

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:15.680
In some stories, leshiis were said to appear
in military uniform, which may have been inspired

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.300
by real fugitive soldiers hiding in the woods.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:24.240
In other cases the leshy is said to approach
humans around a campfire, asking for food.

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:29.450
The forest did historically serve as a place
of shelter for outliers of society.

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:35.250
Perhaps the leshy asking for food is an exaggeration
of such individuals looking for assistance.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:40.150
Most of what we can study about Slavic spirits
now comes from materials recorded in the nineteenth

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:46.050
century when urbanization and advances in
science and education made belief in the supernatural

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:47.050
tenuous.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:53.030
Nevertheless, an 1850’s Russian study found
that “many” peasants claimed to have encountered

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:54.810
a leshy personally.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:59.870
The power of Slavic folklore lasted a long
time, and it can tell us a lot about how the

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:01.440
Slavs saw the world around them.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:05.900
The leshy has become less popular over time,
perhaps because the lessons he teaches are

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:10.560
no longer as relevant, as the forests have
been cleared and rural Slavic life became

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:11.560
less common.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:15.360
While the rituals associated with this guardian
and demon of the forest dwindle, the idea

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.440
of him does appear in popular culture now
and again

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:22.520
Despite what they may tell you, the leshy
is both a guardian and an avenger.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:28.940
Since I know you've spent some time over in Russia and you've done a lot of work with some of these native language texts

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:33.420
Do you still think, or have you encountered people who still believe in the leshy?

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:37.860
We’ve definitely had a resurgence within
the last 20 or 30 years, which is a way of

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:42.120
people I think to get in touch with their
own country, their own history, their own

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.360
landscape.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:47.210
Definitely there’s tons of superstition
in Russia.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:52.420
It’s probably the country that loves superstition
the most of any place I’ve travelled.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:58.260
That can mean unmarried women can’t sit
at the corner of the table, walking under

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:01.640
ladders, cats, giving bread to your household
guardians.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:05.300
As far as someone who believes specifically
in a Leshy, I haven’t met somebody like

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:06.180
that.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:11.160
But I think, I think more people are willing
to believe in the power of nature.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:19.880
So I think believing that the forest has a
presence and a life and a divinity, I think

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:24.500
is certainly real and alive in present Russia.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:29.120
Neither good nor evil, this forest-dwelling
shapeshifter was scary because it could be

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:30.990
lurking around every corner.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:35.550
The leshy represents a deep respect for the
forest and acknowledges the danger humans

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:38.700
encountered there, especially when it was
largely untamed.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:44.240
It was something that could only be avoided
with caution, awareness, and a sincere appreciation

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:45.550
of your surroundings.

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:46.690
The moral of the story?

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:48.370
Be nice to nature.

00:09:48.370 --> 00:10:01.389
You never know when a giant forest spirit
will come for you.

